rota lap 4335, row 1 -- Air, the row that feels; advanced by hand from row 0, which my own last
rota lap had already read today. Its own instruction produced the whole finding: press the fence
rota and see whether the hand passes through. I pressed our own store first and it went straight
rota through -- a content-addressed read that verifies nothing and a buffer that fills in silence.
think Opened by reading MAP, the whole card, the council grid, and the Air threshold page, then
think launched the cold roster pass detached with the --detach flag my own last lap built.
think Took the booked grant in my lane -- table stores, most TAME-aligned scheme, step one, the
think external-research reading. Read the tree's own store before reading anybody else's, because
think Air asks where a thing ends and our own fence was the nearest one.
think mantra/src/store.rye holds four numeric ceilings and no name on any of them, and two of them
think are the same function twice at two heights: store.rye:76 reads 1 MiB, main.rye:209 reads
think 4 MiB, over one .mantra/blobs/ directory, because main.rye imports weave.rye and carries its
think own Store rather than importing store.rye.
think Then the two readings that make it a red rather than a ratchet. Sha3.hash appears twice in
think mantra/src/ and both sites are inside write_blob, so no read path ever verifies the digest.
think And Dir.readFile calls readSliceShort, which returns buffer.len the moment the buffer fills
think -- so a blob past the ceiling comes back as its own first 4 MiB with no error and no signal.
think Followed it downstream: a truncated weave record is a VALID PREFIX, since from_v1 refuses
think falling positions and a generation below one and a prefix violates neither. So it lifts, the
think next mantra add serializes the shortened weave, and the truncation commits under its own
think honest digest. The store reads itself as sound the whole way.
think Then the cold pass reached stash_record at minute 30 and answered unlanded=2 -- and one of
think the two was this grant's paper, already written by a parked lap of my own at 15:13, 360
think lines, grading A/96. I had spent the lap's first hour writing a second one.
obs The instrument that would have prevented it runs at the open, not in the pass:
obs fleet_round_open.sh greps ^unlanded= and prints the dead-letter box count in about a second. I
obs opened by hand with git status instead, and paid an hour for it. Named against myself.
obs Landed the parked paper rather than my duplicate's comparative half, since two papers reaching
obs different conclusions about one grant is worse for a reader than one paper reaching one.
obs Kept my own new section as its own short paper, because the truncation find is independent of
obs the grant and the parked paper reads a different store (Mandate, not Mantra's blob store).
obs Mantra is patchouli's lane, so the repair is sized and handed over rather than taken.
obs The REDS pin refused the row a third day -- pin_headroom=1764, median row 2,898,
obs rows_that_fit=0 -- so the find is carried on the card and in the paper instead.
obs Against myself a second time, and the hot pass caught it: my two index rows went in under
obs the delimiter without checking descending order, so 20260908.151344 stood above
obs 20260908.155443. That reddened index_row_bound as rows_misordered, and dayshelf_merge with
obs it -- the day-shelf merge driver sorts, so a misordered shelf fails its own idempotence leg
obs when merged with itself. One cause, two guards, and neither is a guard I would have thought
obs to run by hand. Moved the row between 152213 and 144500; both green, and the second hot pass
obs closed at 190 green with the same three reds the cold open carried.
obs No zig on PATH here, so every section-2 claim is derived from source read on this bench rather
obs than run on metal, and the paper says so and names the on-metal falsifier.
